success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I can't see the specific forms you reviewed, so this reflects typical market practice.\n\n**Rule 6c-11:** An \"authorized participant\" must be a member or participant of an SEC-registered clearing agency (in practice, DTC/NSCC). It must have a written agreement with **the ETF or one of its service providers**, such as the distributor or transfer agent.\n\n**Typical US forms:** The main signatories are usually the **distributor** (e.g., Foreside, ALPS) and the **AP**. The transfer agent or custodian often signs as an acknowledging party. The **trust** (a Delaware statutory or Massachusetts business trust registered as an open-end fund, with each ETF as a series) is often a named beneficiary or third party rather than the contracting principal.\n\n**Irish ICAV:** The **ICAV itself**, a corporate body with segregated sub-fund liability, usually contracts directly with the AP on behalf of the sub-fund, often alongside the management company. Settlement typically runs through ICSDs (Euroclear/Clearstream) rather than DTC.","ttft_ms":6028,"type":"result","duration_ms":8984,"uuid":"50b6fe1a-132b-414e-b8b2-d0fc012cef15","ttft_stream_ms":1121,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":1121,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
